IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg8-nouns`
IMPORT `dg8-s263-merger-with-partnerships`
IMPORT `dg8-s264-merger-with-llcs`
IMPORT `dg8-s265-conversion-to-a-corporation`
IMPORT `dg8-s266-conversion-to-other-entities`
IMPORT `dg8-s267-parent-and-subsidiary-merger`
IMPORT `dg8-s268-certificate-amendments-and-disclosure-schedules`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter IX, sections 263 to 268 (piece dg8) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online, made by a converter script; it is not the official text
-- and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation Law (an incorporator, a director or officer,
-- a stockholder including a minority stockholder), asking what the Law lets them do, what it requires of them, what they may require of the corporation,
-- and what can be done to them.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the dg8 modules imported above as the questions that person asks when their corporation is merging or
-- consolidating with a partnership or a limited liability company (sections 263 and 264), when an entity is converting to a corporation of this State (265),
-- when their corporation is converting to another entity (266), when an entity that owns 90 percent of their corporation merges it (267), or when the merger
-- agreement is silent on the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation or comes with disclosure schedules (268). Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc
-- worded as the person would be asked. The records the modules expect (the statements in an agreement or certificate, the approvals, the classes of stock, an entity)
-- are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here. A field that a rule never reads
-- is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- Where the existing text hands a judgment to someone else the modules take the judgment as a plain input; this layer asks it the same way:
--   * whether a merger would cause a charitable nonstock corporation's charitable status to be lost or impaired (ss 263(f), 264(f), 266(j));
--   * what the Secretary of State prescribes for service by electronic transmission (ss 263(d), 264(d), 266(c)(6));
--   * the approval of a conversion under the governing writing of the other entity and non-Delaware law (s 265(h), (k)).
-- Several of the answers are only "out of range" facts: the manner of approval under sections 251 and 255, execution under section 103, section 155, the fee under section 391(a)(29).
-- They are asked as yes/no facts; the pieces that encode those sections decide them.
--
-- Section 267 asks the 90 percent test as one class: the person states the shares outstanding and the shares the parent owns of the class the parent owns the smallest share of.
-- That single class stands for "each class" (if the parent reaches 90 percent of the class it owns least of, it reaches it in every class). Assumed, not ruled (NOTES.md).
--
-- Section 114(b)(2) takes section 267 out of the reading of "stockholder" as "member" for a nonstock corporation; sections 263 to 266 and 268 are read with that reading.

§ `The entities the person may be asking about`

-- A flat choice of what an entity is, for the sections whose rules take an entity (265(a), 266(a)) or a kind of entity (263(a), 264(a), 267(d)).
-- Not law: it only builds the core's Kind of entity and Entity from one answer.
DECLARE `dg8 seat Entity the person describes` IS ONE OF
    `entity that is a limited liability company`
    `entity that is a statutory trust`
    `entity that is a business trust or association`
    `entity that is a real estate investment trust`
    `entity that is a common-law trust`
    `entity that is a general partnership`
    `entity that is a limited partnership`
    `entity that is a limited liability partnership`
    `entity that is a limited liability limited partnership`
    `entity that is a joint-stock association`
    `entity that is any other unincorporated business or association`
    `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of Delaware`
    `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of another State or territory of the United States`
    `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of a foreign country`
    `entity that is a natural person`

-- A corporation's own kind (stock, nonstock) is not read by sections 265(a), 266(a) or 267(d)(2): the placeholder `a stock corporation` is fixed.
GIVEN x IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes`
GIVETH A `Kind of entity`
`dg8 seat the kind of entity described` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `entity that is a limited liability company` THEN `a limited liability company`
    WHEN `entity that is a statutory trust` THEN `a statutory trust`
    WHEN `entity that is a business trust or association` THEN `a business trust or association`
    WHEN `entity that is a real estate investment trust` THEN `a real estate investment trust`
    WHEN `entity that is a common-law trust` THEN `a common-law trust`
    WHEN `entity that is a general partnership` THEN `a general partnership`
    WHEN `entity that is a limited partnership` THEN `a limited partnership`
    WHEN `entity that is a limited liability partnership` THEN `a limited liability partnership`
    WHEN `entity that is a limited liability limited partnership` THEN `a limited liability limited partnership`
    WHEN `entity that is a joint-stock association` THEN `a joint-stock association`
    WHEN `entity that is any other unincorporated business or association` THEN `any other unincorporated business or association`
    WHEN `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of Delaware` THEN `a corporation` `a stock corporation`
    WHEN `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of another State or territory of the United States` THEN `a corporation` `a stock corporation`
    WHEN `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of a foreign country` THEN `a corporation` `a stock corporation`
    WHEN `entity that is a natural person` THEN `a natural person`

-- Where the entity is formed is read only for a corporation (is it a corporation of this State?), by sections 265(a) and 266(a); for every other kind the placeholder `this State` is fixed.
-- For a natural person "where formed" has no meaning (core note): the same placeholder.
GIVEN x IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes`
GIVETH AN Entity
`dg8 seat the entity described` x MEANS
    Entity WITH `kind of entity` IS `dg8 seat the kind of entity described` x
              , `where formed` IS
                    CONSIDER x
                    WHEN `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of another State or territory of the United States` THEN `another jurisdiction of the United States`
                    WHEN `entity that is a corporation formed under the laws of a foreign country` THEN `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
                    OTHERWISE `this State`


§ `s 263 -- my corporation merging or consolidating with a partnership`

-- This group arises only if a corporation of this State is merging or consolidating with one or more partnerships.

-- s 263(a). A corporation of this State may merge or consolidate with one or more partnerships unless the law of the partnership's jurisdiction prohibits it.
-- The corporation's power is the partnership's liability to be merged with it; the partnership's own law may deny the power.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(a)
@export May my corporation merge or consolidate with one or more partnerships (s 263(a))?
GIVEN `the number of Delaware corporations that are to merge or consolidate` IS A NUMBER @desc How many corporations of Delaware, counting mine, are to merge or consolidate?
      `the number of partnerships that are to merge or consolidate` IS A NUMBER @desc How many partnerships are to merge or consolidate with them?
      `the law of a partnership's jurisdiction prohibits the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the laws of the jurisdiction under which any of those partnerships is formed prohibit the merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation merge or consolidate with partnerships (s 263(a))` IS
    `s 263(a) corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with partnerships` `the number of Delaware corporations that are to merge or consolidate` `the number of partnerships that are to merge or consolidate` `the law of a partnership's jurisdiction prohibits the merger or consolidation`

-- s 263(a). "Partnership" in this section: a general partnership (including a limited liability partnership) or a limited partnership (including a limited liability limited partnership), formed under the laws of any jurisdiction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(a)
@export Is my entity a partnership within the meaning of section 263 (s 263(a))?
GIVEN `what my entity is` IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes` @desc What kind of entity is it? Choose the description that fits.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my entity a partnership within section 263 (s 263(a))` IS
    `s 263(a) the term partnership` (`dg8 seat the kind of entity described` `what my entity is`)

-- s 263(b). Each corporation and partnership enters into a written agreement that states (1) the terms, (2) the mode, (3) for a merger into a surviving corporation the changes to its certificate of incorporation,
-- (4) for a consolidation into a resulting corporation its certificate, (5) the manner of converting or cancelling shares and interests and what holders are to receive, and (7) what each partnership's law requires.
-- The duty to include them is on the constituents; for a stockholder it is a statement the agreement must make to them.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b)
@export Does our written agreement of merger or consolidation state everything section 263(b) requires (s 263(b))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `each constituent has entered into a written agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each corporation and each partnership entered into a written agreement of merger or consolidation?
      `some shares or interests are not to remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any shares or partnership interests not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into securities of the surviving or resulting entity or to be cancelled?
      `the holders of those are to receive other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holders of those shares or interests to receive cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity?
      `the agreement states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation?
      `the agreement states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect?
      `the agreement states the changes to the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a corporation of this State survives a merger: does the agreement state the amendments or changes in its certificate of incorporation, or that its certificate of incorporation shall be its certificate of incorporation?
      `the agreement states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a new corporation of this State results from a consolidation: does the agreement state that its certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment to the agreement?
      `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling the shares and interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock and the partnership interests into securities of the surviving or resulting entity, or of cancelling some or all of them?
      `the agreement states what the other holders are to receive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity that the holders of shares or interests not to remain outstanding are to receive?
      `the agreement sets out what the law of each partnership's jurisdiction requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement set out the other provisions or facts that the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the partnerships are formed require?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 263(b) requires (s 263(b))` IS
    `s 263(b) the agreement of merger or consolidation is as the subsection requires` `each constituent has entered into a written agreement` `the form of the combination` `some shares or interests are not to remain outstanding` `the holders of those are to receive other consideration` `my statements`
    WHERE
        `my statements` MEANS `s 263(b) Statements in the agreement of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `s 263(b)(1) the agreement states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation` IS `the agreement states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`
            `s 263(b)(2) the agreement states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect` IS `the agreement states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`
            `s 263(b)(3) the agreement states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation` IS `the agreement states the changes to the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is`
            `s 263(b)(4) the agreement states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the agreement` IS `the agreement states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as attached`
            `s 263(b)(5) the agreement states the manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock and the partnership interests into securities of the surviving or resulting entity, or of cancelling some or all of them` IS `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling the shares and interests`
            `s 263(b)(5) the agreement states the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity that the holders of shares or interests not to remain outstanding are to receive` IS `the agreement states what the other holders are to receive`
            `s 263(b)(7) the agreement sets out the other provisions or facts that the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the partnerships are formed require` IS `the agreement sets out what the law of each partnership's jurisdiction requires`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b)
@export May a term of our agreement of merger or consolidation depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement (s 263(b))?
GIVEN `the term depends on facts outside the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement?
      `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those facts operate on the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a term of our agreement depend on facts outside the agreement (s 263(b))` IS
    `s 263(b) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the term depends on facts outside the agreement` `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b)(6)
@export May our agreement include a detail or provision we think desirable, such as cash in place of fractional shares (s 263(b)(6))?
GIVEN `we think the detail or provision desirable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the constituents deem the detail or provision desirable?
      `it deals with fractional shares, rights, securities or interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests, or some other arrangement for them?
      `the arrangement is consistent with section 155` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement for fractions consistent with section 155 of the Law? (Answer no if you are unsure, or if it does not deal with fractions it does not matter.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our agreement include this detail or provision (s 263(b)(6))` IS
    `s 263(b)(6) the detail or provision may be included in the agreement` `we think the detail or provision desirable` `it deals with fractional shares, rights, securities or interests` `the arrangement is consistent with section 155`

-- s 263(c). If the survivor is a partnership, each stockholder of a merging corporation who will become a general partner of it must approve, in addition to any other approvals.
-- The stockholder's approval is a condition of the agreement; the corporation cannot make the stockholder a general partner without it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c)
@export Must I approve the agreement of merger or consolidation because I would become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership (s 263(c))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `I will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you, as a stockholder of a merging corporation, become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I approve the merger or consolidation because I would become a general partner (s 263(c))` IS
    `s 263(c) the stockholder must approve the agreement` `the form of the combination` `I will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership`

-- s 263(c). Each corporation approves as under section 251 or 255; each partnership as its partnership agreement and law provide.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c)
@export Has our agreement of merger or consolidation been adopted and approved as section 263(c) requires (s 263(c))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `each corporation has adopted and approved the agreement as section 251 or 255 provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each corporation adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in the same manner as is provided in section 251 or section 255 of the Law?
      `each partnership has approved the agreement under its partnership agreement and law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each partnership adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in accordance with its partnership agreement and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed?
      `a stockholder will become a general partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will any stockholder of a merging corporation become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership?
      `each such stockholder has approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each such stockholder approved the agreement? (Answer yes if there is no such stockholder.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has our agreement been approved as section 263(c) requires (s 263(c))` IS
    `s 263(c) the agreement has the approvals the subsection requires` `the form of the combination` `the approvals`
    WHERE
        `the approvals` MEANS `s 263(c) Approvals of the agreement` WITH
            `s 263(c) each corporation has adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in the same manner as is provided in § 251 or § 255` IS `each corporation has adopted and approved the agreement as section 251 or 255 provides`
            `s 263(c) each partnership has adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in accordance with its partnership agreement and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed` IS `each partnership has approved the agreement under its partnership agreement and law`
            `s 263(c) a stockholder of a merging corporation will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership` IS `a stockholder will become a general partner`
            `s 263(c) each stockholder who will become a general partner of the surviving or resulting partnership has approved the agreement` IS `each such stockholder has approved`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c)
@export Has the merger or consolidation taken effect for all purposes of the laws of Delaware on the day I am asking about (s 263(c))?
GIVEN `the agreement, or a certificate in its place, has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the agreement of merger or consolidation, or a certificate of merger or consolidation filed in its place, been filed?
      `the date it takes effect under section 251 or 255` IS A DATE @desc On what date does it become effective as section 251 or section 255 of the Law provides? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking whether it is in effect? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the merger or consolidation in effect under the laws of Delaware (s 263(c))` IS
    `s 263(c) the merger or consolidation is effective for all purposes of the laws of this State` `the agreement, or a certificate in its place, has been filed` `the date it takes effect under section 251 or 255` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 263(c). In place of filing the agreement the survivor may file a certificate of merger or consolidation, executed under section 103 if the survivor is a corporation or by a general partner if a partnership, stating (1) to (8).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c)
@export May the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 263(c))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting partnership formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware? (Answer no if the survivor is a corporation.)
      `the certificate states the name, jurisdiction and type of entity of each constituent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name, jurisdiction of formation or organization and type of entity of each of the constituent entities?
      `the certificate states that each constituent approved the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent entities?
      `the certificate states the name of the survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name of the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership?
      `the certificate states the changes to the surviving corporation certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a corporation survives a merger: does the certificate state the amendments or changes in its certificate of incorporation, or that its certificate of incorporation shall be its certificate of incorporation?
      `the certificate states that the resulting corporation certificate is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a new corporation results from a consolidation: does the certificate state that its certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment to the certificate?
      `the certificate states that the agreement is on file and where` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership, and the address of that office?
      `the certificate states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that a copy of the agreement will be furnished, on request and without cost, to any stockholder of any constituent corporation or any partner of any constituent partnership?
      `the certificate states the agreement required by subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the agreement, if any, required by subsection (d) (the agreement to be served with process in Delaware)?
      `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a corporation survives: was the certificate executed in accordance with section 103 of the Law?
      `the certificate was executed by a general partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a partnership survives: was the certificate executed by a general partner of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 263(c))` IS
    `s 263(c) the certificate of merger or consolidation may be filed in lieu of the agreement` (`s 263(c) the certificate is executed as the subsection requires` `the form of the combination` `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103` `the certificate was executed by a general partner`) (`s 263(c) the certificate states what the subsection requires` `the form of the combination` `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed outside Delaware` `the certificate statements`)
    WHERE
        `the certificate statements` MEANS `s 263(c) Statements in the certificate of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `s 263(c)(1) the certificate states the name, jurisdiction of formation or organization and type of entity of each of the constituent entities` IS `the certificate states the name, jurisdiction and type of entity of each constituent`
            `s 263(c)(2) the certificate states that an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent entities in accordance with the subsection` IS `the certificate states that each constituent approved the agreement`
            `s 263(c)(3) the certificate states the name of the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership` IS `the certificate states the name of the survivor`
            `s 263(c)(4) the certificate states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that its certificate of incorporation shall be its certificate of incorporation` IS `the certificate states the changes to the surviving corporation certificate of incorporation`
            `s 263(c)(5) the certificate states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the certificate` IS `the certificate states that the resulting corporation certificate is attached`
            `s 263(c)(6) the certificate states that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation or partnership and the address of that office` IS `the certificate states that the agreement is on file and where`
            `s 263(c)(7) the certificate states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished, on request and without cost, to any stockholder of any constituent corporation or any partner of any constituent partnership` IS `the certificate states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished free`
            `s 263(c)(8) the certificate states the agreement, if any, required by subsection (d)` IS `the certificate states the agreement required by subsection (d)`

-- s 263(c)(7). The stockholder's or partner's claim to a copy is the surviving entity's duty to furnish it. The claim is read as arising where a certificate was filed in place of the agreement (fork F6).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(c)(7)
@export Can I have a copy of the agreement of merger or consolidation from the surviving or resulting entity, on request and without cost (s 263(c)(7))?
GIVEN `I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of a constituent corporation?
      `I am a partner of a constituent partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a partner of a constituent partnership?
      `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in place of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of merger or consolidation filed in place of the agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I get a copy of the merger agreement on request and without cost (s 263(c)(7))` IS
    `s 263(c)(7) the person may have a copy of the agreement on request and without cost` `I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation` `I am a partner of a constituent partnership` `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in place of the agreement`

-- s 263(d). The survivor's agreement to be served is the claimant's power to serve it through the Secretary of State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export Must the surviving or resulting partnership agree that it may be served with process in Delaware (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting partnership formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the surviving partnership agree to be served with process in Delaware (s 263(d))` IS
    `s 263(d) the surviving or resulting partnership must agree to be served with process in this State` `the form of the combination` `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed outside Delaware`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export Has the surviving or resulting partnership agreed to be served with process in Delaware as section 263(d) requires (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting partnership formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
      `it agrees to be served for the obligations of a constituent of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the partnership agree that it may be served with process in Delaware in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent corporation or partnership of this State?
      `it agrees to be served for its own obligations arising from the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the partnership agree that it may be served with process in Delaware in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting partnership arising from the merger or consolidation, including a suit to enforce the right of stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings under section 262?
      `it irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the partnership irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings?
      `it specifies the address for the Secretary of State to mail a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the partnership specify the address to which a copy of such process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the surviving partnership agreed to be served as section 263(d) requires (s 263(d))` IS
    `s 263(d) the surviving or resulting partnership has agreed as the subsection requires` `the form of the combination` `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed outside Delaware` `its agreement`
    WHERE
        `its agreement` MEANS `s 263(d) Statements in the agreement to be served with process` WITH
            `s 263(d) the partnership agrees that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent corporation or partnership of this State` IS `it agrees to be served for the obligations of a constituent of Delaware`
            `s 263(d) the partnership agrees that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting partnership arising from the merger or consolidation, including any suit or other proceeding to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to § 262` IS `it agrees to be served for its own obligations arising from the merger`
            `s 263(d) the partnership irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings` IS `it irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent`
            `s 263(d) the partnership specifies the address to which a copy of such process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State` IS `it specifies the address for the Secretary of State to mail a copy`

-- s 263(d). The claimant's power to serve the Secretary of State is the survivor's liability to be served there (fork F7).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export May I serve process on the Secretary of State, as agent of the surviving or resulting partnership, in my proceeding (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting partnership formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
      `my proceeding is to enforce a constituent's obligation or the survivor's obligation from the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your proceeding to enforce an obligation of a constituent corporation or partnership of Delaware, or an obligation of the surviving or resulting partnership arising from the merger or consolidation (including an appraisal suit)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I serve process on the Secretary of State to sue the surviving partnership (s 263(d))` IS
    `s 263(d) process may be served on the Secretary of State as agent of the surviving or resulting partnership` `the form of the combination` `the surviving or resulting partnership is formed outside Delaware` `my proceeding is to enforce a constituent's obligation or the survivor's obligation from the merger`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export May I serve process on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `I serve by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you serve the process by electronic transmission?
      `I serve as the Secretary of State prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you serve it as the Secretary of State has prescribed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 263(d))` IS
    `s 263(d) the means of serving process on the Secretary of State is permitted` `I serve by electronic transmission` `I serve as the Secretary of State prescribes`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export Must the Secretary of State forthwith notify the surviving or resulting partnership by letter of the service (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `process has been served on the Secretary of State under the subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has process been served on the Secretary of State under section 263(d)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary of State notify the surviving partnership by letter (s 263(d))` IS
    `s 263(d) the Secretary of State must forthwith notify the surviving or resulting partnership by letter` `process has been served on the Secretary of State under the subsection`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter of notice (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `the address the partnership specified` IS A STRING @desc What address did the surviving or resulting partnership specify for the Secretary of State to mail process to?
      `the addresses designated in writing since, oldest first` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc What different addresses has it since designated in writing to the Secretary of State, oldest first? (An empty list if none.)
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter (s 263(d))` IS
    `s 263(d) the address to which the Secretary of State must mail the letter` `the address the partnership specified` `the addresses designated in writing since, oldest first`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export Was the Secretary of State's letter sent as the Law requires (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `it was sent by a mail or courier service with records of mailing and signed delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient?
      `it enclosed a copy of the process and papers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the letter enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the Secretary of State's letter sent as section 263(d) requires (s 263(d))` IS
    `s 263(d) the letter is sent as the subsection requires` `it was sent by a mail or courier service with records of mailing and signed delivery` `it enclosed a copy of the process and papers`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export Have I done what the Law requires of a plaintiff who serves the Secretary of State (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `I served process and papers in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve process and any other papers in duplicate?
      `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under the subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected under section 263(d)?
      `I paid the Secretary of State the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done what section 263(d) requires of a plaintiff (s 263(d))` IS
    `s 263(d) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires of a plaintiff` `I served process and papers in duplicate` `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under the subsection` `I paid the Secretary of State the prescribed fee`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs if I prevail (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `I prevail in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you prevail in the proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State be taxed as costs (s 263(d))` IS
    `s 263(d) the fee is taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding` `I prevail in the proceeding`

-- s 263(d). The Secretary of State need not retain the record longer than 5 years from receipt (the fifth anniversary is still inside the period).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(d)
@export Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on a given day (s 263(d))?
GIVEN `the date the Secretary of State received the service` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State receive the service of process? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service (s 263(d))` IS
    NOT (`s 263(d) the Secretary of State is no longer required to retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service` `the day I am asking about`)

-- s 263(b). "Facts" includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
-- The list is open: an event, a determination or an action is a fact; for anything else the text does not say (the answer is then NOTHING).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(b)
@export Is this kind of fact one that a term of our agreement of merger or consolidation may depend on, under the meaning of "facts" in section 263(b) (s 263(b))?
GIVEN `the kind of fact` IS A `s 263(b) Kind of fact` @desc Which kind of fact? One of: the occurrence of an event under s 263(b); a determination by any person or body, including the corporation, under s 263(b); an action by any person or body, including the corporation, under s 263(b); something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 263(b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a fact a term of our agreement may depend on (s 263(b))` IS
    `s 263(b) the kind of fact is within the term facts` `the kind of fact`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(e)
@export Does this provision of the Law apply to a merger or consolidation between a corporation and a partnership (s 263(e))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `s 263(e) Provision applied by reference` @desc Which provision? One of: s 251(d) to (f) as applied by s 263(e); s 255(c) second sentence and (d) to (f) as applied by s 263(e); ss 259 to 261 as applied by s 263(e); s 328 as applied by s 263(e)
      `it is applicable to my merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision applicable to your merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision apply to a merger between a corporation and a partnership (s 263(e))` IS
    `s 263(e) the provision applies to the merger or consolidation` `the provision` `it is applicable to my merger or consolidation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(f)
@export Does section 263 stop my corporation merging into a partnership because its charitable status would be lost or impaired (s 263(f))?
GIVEN `the kind of my corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it? One of: a stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; a charitable nonstock corporation
      `my corporation would be merged into the partnership and would not survive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your corporation be merged into the partnership, so that it does not continue as the surviving corporation?
      `its charitable status would be lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the merger cause its charitable status to be lost or impaired?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 263 stop my charitable nonstock corporation merging into a partnership (s 263(f))` IS
    `s 263(f) the section does not authorize the merger of the charitable nonstock corporation into the partnership` `the kind of my corporation` `my corporation would be merged into the partnership and would not survive` `its charitable status would be lost or impaired`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 263(f)
@export May a partnership be merged into my charitable nonstock corporation, which continues as the surviving corporation (s 263(f))?
GIVEN `the kind of my corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it? One of: a stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; a charitable nonstock corporation
      `my corporation continues as the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your corporation continue as the surviving corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a partnership be merged into my charitable nonstock corporation (s 263(f))` IS
    `s 263(f) the partnership may be merged into the charitable nonstock corporation` `the kind of my corporation` `my corporation continues as the surviving corporation`


§ `s 264 -- my corporation merging or consolidating with a limited liability company`

-- This group arises only if a corporation of this State is merging or consolidating with one or more limited liability companies.

-- s 264(a). A corporation of this State may merge or consolidate with one or more limited liability companies unless the law of the limited liability company's jurisdiction prohibits it.
-- The corporation's power is the limited liability company's liability to be merged with it; the limited liability company's own law may deny the power.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(a)
@export May my corporation merge or consolidate with one or more limited liability companies (s 264(a))?
GIVEN `the number of Delaware corporations that are to merge or consolidate` IS A NUMBER @desc How many corporations of Delaware, counting mine, are to merge or consolidate?
      `the number of limited liability companies that are to merge or consolidate` IS A NUMBER @desc How many limited liability companies are to merge or consolidate with them?
      `the law of a limited liability company's jurisdiction prohibits the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the laws of the jurisdiction under which any of those limited liability companies is formed prohibit the merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation merge or consolidate with limited liability companies (s 264(a))` IS
    `s 264(a) corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with limited liability companies` `the number of Delaware corporations that are to merge or consolidate` `the number of limited liability companies that are to merge or consolidate` `the law of a limited liability company's jurisdiction prohibits the merger or consolidation`

-- s 264(a). "Limited liability company" in this section: any limited liability company formed under the laws of this State or of any other jurisdiction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(a)
@export Is my entity a limited liability company within the meaning of section 264 (s 264(a))?
GIVEN `what my entity is` IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes` @desc What kind of entity is it? Choose the description that fits.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my entity a limited liability company within section 264 (s 264(a))` IS
    `s 264(a) the term limited liability company` (`dg8 seat the kind of entity described` `what my entity is`)

-- s 264(b). Each corporation and limited liability company enters into a written agreement that states (1) the terms, (2) the mode, (3) for a merger into a surviving corporation the changes to its certificate of incorporation,
-- (4) for a consolidation into a resulting corporation its certificate, (5) the manner of converting or cancelling shares and interests and what holders are to receive, and (7) what each limited liability company's law requires.
-- The duty to include them is on the constituents; for a stockholder it is a statement the agreement must make to them.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(b)
@export Does our written agreement of merger or consolidation state everything section 264(b) requires (s 264(b))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `each constituent has entered into a written agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each corporation and each limited liability company entered into a written agreement of merger or consolidation?
      `some shares or interests are not to remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any shares or limited liability company interests not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into securities of the surviving or resulting entity or to be cancelled?
      `the holders of those are to receive other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holders of those shares or interests to receive cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity?
      `the agreement states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation?
      `the agreement states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect?
      `the agreement states the changes to the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a corporation of this State survives a merger: does the agreement state the amendments or changes in its certificate of incorporation, or that its certificate of incorporation shall be its certificate of incorporation?
      `the agreement states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a new corporation of this State results from a consolidation: does the agreement state that its certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment to the agreement?
      `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling the shares and interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock and the limited liability company interests into securities of the surviving or resulting entity, or of cancelling some or all of them?
      `the agreement states what the other holders are to receive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity that the holders of shares or interests not to remain outstanding are to receive?
      `the agreement sets out what the law of each partnership's jurisdiction requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement set out the other provisions or facts that the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the limited liability companies are formed require?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our agreement of merger or consolidation state what section 264(b) requires (s 264(b))` IS
    `s 264(b) the agreement of merger or consolidation is as the subsection requires` `each constituent has entered into a written agreement` `the form of the combination` `some shares or interests are not to remain outstanding` `the holders of those are to receive other consideration` `my statements`
    WHERE
        `my statements` MEANS `s 264(b) Statements in the agreement of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `s 264(b)(1) the agreement states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation` IS `the agreement states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`
            `s 264(b)(2) the agreement states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect` IS `the agreement states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`
            `s 264(b)(3) the agreement states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation` IS `the agreement states the changes to the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is`
            `s 264(b)(4) the agreement states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the agreement` IS `the agreement states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as attached`
            `s 264(b)(5) the agreement states the manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock and the limited liability company interests into securities of the surviving or resulting entity, or of cancelling some or all of them` IS `the agreement states the manner of converting or cancelling the shares and interests`
            `s 264(b)(5) the agreement states the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity that the holders of shares or interests not to remain outstanding are to receive` IS `the agreement states what the other holders are to receive`
            `s 264(b)(7) the agreement sets out the other provisions or facts that the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the limited liability companies are formed require` IS `the agreement sets out what the law of each partnership's jurisdiction requires`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(b)
@export May a term of our agreement of merger or consolidation depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement (s 264(b))?
GIVEN `the term depends on facts outside the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement?
      `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those facts operate on the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a term of our agreement depend on facts outside the agreement (s 264(b))` IS
    `s 264(b) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the term depends on facts outside the agreement` `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(b)(6)
@export May our agreement include a detail or provision we think desirable, such as cash in place of fractional shares (s 264(b)(6))?
GIVEN `we think the detail or provision desirable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the constituents deem the detail or provision desirable?
      `it deals with fractional shares, rights, securities or interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests, or some other arrangement for them?
      `the arrangement is consistent with section 155` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrangement for fractions consistent with section 155 of the Law? (Answer no if you are unsure, or if it does not deal with fractions it does not matter.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our agreement include this detail or provision (s 264(b)(6))` IS
    `s 264(b)(6) the detail or provision may be included in the agreement` `we think the detail or provision desirable` `it deals with fractional shares, rights, securities or interests` `the arrangement is consistent with section 155`

-- s 264(c). Each corporation approves as under section 251 or 255; each limited liability company as its limited liability company agreement and law provide.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(c)
@export Has our agreement of merger or consolidation been adopted and approved as section 264(c) requires (s 264(c))?
GIVEN `each corporation has adopted and approved the agreement as section 251 or 255 provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each corporation adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in the same manner as is provided in section 251 or section 255 of the Law?
      `each limited liability company has approved the agreement under its limited liability company agreement and law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each limited liability company adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in accordance with its limited liability company agreement and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has our agreement been approved as section 264(c) requires (s 264(c))` IS
    `s 264(c) the agreement has the approvals the subsection requires` `the approvals`
    WHERE
        `the approvals` MEANS `s 264(c) Approvals of the agreement` WITH
            `s 264(c) each corporation has adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in the same manner as is provided in § 251 or § 255` IS `each corporation has adopted and approved the agreement as section 251 or 255 provides`
            `s 264(c) each limited liability company has adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement in accordance with its limited liability company agreement and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed` IS `each limited liability company has approved the agreement under its limited liability company agreement and law`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(c)
@export Has the merger or consolidation taken effect for all purposes of the laws of Delaware on the day I am asking about (s 264(c))?
GIVEN `the agreement, or a certificate in its place, has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the agreement of merger or consolidation, or a certificate of merger or consolidation filed in its place, been filed?
      `the date it takes effect under section 251 or 255` IS A DATE @desc On what date does it become effective as section 251 or section 255 of the Law provides? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking whether it is in effect? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the merger or consolidation in effect under the laws of Delaware (s 264(c))` IS
    `s 264(c) the merger or consolidation is effective for all purposes of the laws of this State` `the agreement, or a certificate in its place, has been filed` `the date it takes effect under section 251 or 255` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 264(c). In place of filing the agreement the survivor may file a certificate of merger or consolidation, executed under section 103 if the survivor is a corporation or by a authorized person if a limited liability company, stating (1) to (8).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(c)
@export May the surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 264(c))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting limited liability company formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware? (Answer no if the survivor is a corporation.)
      `the certificate states the name and jurisdiction of each constituent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name and jurisdiction of formation or organization of each of the constituent entities?
      `the certificate states that each constituent approved the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent entities?
      `the certificate states the name of the survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name of the surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company?
      `the certificate states the changes to the surviving corporation certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a corporation survives a merger: does the certificate state the amendments or changes in its certificate of incorporation, or that its certificate of incorporation shall be its certificate of incorporation?
      `the certificate states that the resulting corporation certificate is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a new corporation results from a consolidation: does the certificate state that its certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment to the certificate?
      `the certificate states that the agreement is on file and where` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company, and the address of that office?
      `the certificate states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that a copy of the agreement will be furnished, on request and without cost, to any stockholder of any constituent corporation or any member of any constituent limited liability company?
      `the certificate states the agreement required by subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the agreement, if any, required by subsection (d) (the agreement to be served with process in Delaware)?
      `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a corporation survives: was the certificate executed in accordance with section 103 of the Law?
      `the certificate was executed by a authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a limited liability company survives: was the certificate executed by an authorized person of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we file a certificate of merger or consolidation instead of the agreement (s 264(c))` IS
    `s 264(c) the certificate of merger or consolidation may be filed in lieu of the agreement` (`s 264(c) the certificate is executed as the subsection requires` `the form of the combination` `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103` `the certificate was executed by a authorized person`) (`s 264(c) the certificate states what the subsection requires` `the form of the combination` `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed outside Delaware` `the certificate statements`)
    WHERE
        `the certificate statements` MEANS `s 264(c) Statements in the certificate of merger or consolidation` WITH
            `s 264(c)(1) the certificate states the name and jurisdiction of formation or organization of each of the constituent entities` IS `the certificate states the name and jurisdiction of each constituent`
            `s 264(c)(2) the certificate states that an agreement of merger or consolidation has been approved, adopted, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent entities in accordance with the subsection` IS `the certificate states that each constituent approved the agreement`
            `s 264(c)(3) the certificate states the name of the surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company` IS `the certificate states the name of the survivor`
            `s 264(c)(4) the certificate states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that its certificate of incorporation shall be its certificate of incorporation` IS `the certificate states the changes to the surviving corporation certificate of incorporation`
            `s 264(c)(5) the certificate states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the certificate` IS `the certificate states that the resulting corporation certificate is attached`
            `s 264(c)(6) the certificate states that the executed agreement is on file at an office of the surviving or resulting corporation or limited liability company and the address of that office` IS `the certificate states that the agreement is on file and where`
            `s 264(c)(7) the certificate states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished, on request and without cost, to any stockholder of any constituent corporation or any member of any constituent limited liability company` IS `the certificate states that a copy of the agreement will be furnished free`
            `s 264(c)(8) the certificate states the agreement, if any, required by subsection (d)` IS `the certificate states the agreement required by subsection (d)`

-- s 264(c)(7). The stockholder's or member's claim to a copy is the surviving entity's duty to furnish it. The claim is read as arising where a certificate was filed in place of the agreement (fork F6).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(c)(7)
@export Can I have a copy of the agreement of merger or consolidation from the surviving or resulting entity, on request and without cost (s 264(c)(7))?
GIVEN `I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of a constituent corporation?
      `I am a member of a constituent limited liability company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a constituent limited liability company?
      `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in place of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of merger or consolidation filed in place of the agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I get a copy of the merger agreement on request and without cost (s 264(c)(7))` IS
    `s 264(c)(7) the person may have a copy of the agreement on request and without cost` `I am a stockholder of a constituent corporation` `I am a member of a constituent limited liability company` `a certificate of merger or consolidation was filed in place of the agreement`

-- s 264(d). The survivor's agreement to be served is the claimant's power to serve it through the Secretary of State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export Must the surviving or resulting limited liability company agree that it may be served with process in Delaware (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting limited liability company formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the surviving limited liability company agree to be served with process in Delaware (s 264(d))` IS
    `s 264(d) the surviving or resulting limited liability company must agree to be served with process in this State` `the form of the combination` `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed outside Delaware`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export Has the surviving or resulting limited liability company agreed to be served with process in Delaware as section 264(d) requires (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting limited liability company formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
      `it agrees to be served for the obligations of a constituent of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the limited liability company agree that it may be served with process in Delaware in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent corporation or limited liability company of this State?
      `it agrees to be served for its own obligations arising from the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the limited liability company agree that it may be served with process in Delaware in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting limited liability company arising from the merger or consolidation, including a suit to enforce the right of stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings under section 262?
      `it irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the limited liability company irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings?
      `it specifies the address for the Secretary of State to mail a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the limited liability company specify the address to which a copy of such process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the surviving limited liability company agreed to be served as section 264(d) requires (s 264(d))` IS
    `s 264(d) the surviving or resulting limited liability company has agreed as the subsection requires` `the form of the combination` `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed outside Delaware` `its agreement`
    WHERE
        `its agreement` MEANS `s 264(d) Statements in the agreement to be served with process` WITH
            `s 264(d) the limited liability company agrees that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent corporation or limited liability company of this State` IS `it agrees to be served for the obligations of a constituent of Delaware`
            `s 264(d) the limited liability company agrees that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting limited liability company arising from the merger or consolidation, including any suit or other proceeding to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to § 262` IS `it agrees to be served for its own obligations arising from the merger`
            `s 264(d) the limited liability company irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings` IS `it irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent`
            `s 264(d) the limited liability company specifies the address to which a copy of such process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State` IS `it specifies the address for the Secretary of State to mail a copy`

-- s 264(d). The claimant's power to serve the Secretary of State is the survivor's liability to be served there (fork F7).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export May I serve process on the Secretary of State, as agent of the surviving or resulting limited liability company, in my proceeding (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `the form of the combination` IS A `dg8 Form of a combination` @desc What form does the combination take? One of: a merger into a surviving corporation of this State; a merger into a surviving entity that is not a corporation; a consolidation into a new resulting corporation of this State; a consolidation into a new resulting entity that is not a corporation
      `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting limited liability company formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
      `my proceeding is to enforce a constituent's obligation or the survivor's obligation from the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your proceeding to enforce an obligation of a constituent corporation or limited liability company of Delaware, or an obligation of the surviving or resulting limited liability company arising from the merger or consolidation (including an appraisal suit)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I serve process on the Secretary of State to sue the surviving limited liability company (s 264(d))` IS
    `s 264(d) process may be served on the Secretary of State as agent of the surviving or resulting limited liability company` `the form of the combination` `the surviving or resulting limited liability company is formed outside Delaware` `my proceeding is to enforce a constituent's obligation or the survivor's obligation from the merger`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export May I serve process on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `I serve by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you serve the process by electronic transmission?
      `I serve as the Secretary of State prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you serve it as the Secretary of State has prescribed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 264(d))` IS
    `s 264(d) the means of serving process on the Secretary of State is permitted` `I serve by electronic transmission` `I serve as the Secretary of State prescribes`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export Must the Secretary of State forthwith notify the surviving or resulting limited liability company by letter of the service (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `process has been served on the Secretary of State under the subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has process been served on the Secretary of State under section 263(d)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary of State notify the surviving limited liability company by letter (s 264(d))` IS
    `s 264(d) the Secretary of State must forthwith notify the surviving or resulting limited liability company by letter` `process has been served on the Secretary of State under the subsection`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter of notice (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `the address the limited liability company specified` IS A STRING @desc What address did the surviving or resulting limited liability company specify for the Secretary of State to mail process to?
      `the addresses designated in writing since, oldest first` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc What different addresses has it since designated in writing to the Secretary of State, oldest first? (An empty list if none.)
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter (s 264(d))` IS
    `s 264(d) the address to which the Secretary of State must mail the letter` `the address the limited liability company specified` `the addresses designated in writing since, oldest first`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export Was the Secretary of State's letter sent as the Law requires (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `it was sent by a mail or courier service with records of mailing and signed delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient?
      `it enclosed a copy of the process and papers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the letter enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the Secretary of State's letter sent as section 264(d) requires (s 264(d))` IS
    `s 264(d) the letter is sent as the subsection requires` `it was sent by a mail or courier service with records of mailing and signed delivery` `it enclosed a copy of the process and papers`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export Have I done what the Law requires of a plaintiff who serves the Secretary of State (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `I served process and papers in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve process and any other papers in duplicate?
      `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under the subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected under section 263(d)?
      `I paid the Secretary of State the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done what section 264(d) requires of a plaintiff (s 264(d))` IS
    `s 264(d) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires of a plaintiff` `I served process and papers in duplicate` `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under the subsection` `I paid the Secretary of State the prescribed fee`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs if I prevail (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `I prevail in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you prevail in the proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State be taxed as costs (s 264(d))` IS
    `s 264(d) the fee is taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding` `I prevail in the proceeding`

-- s 264(d). The Secretary of State need not retain the record longer than 5 years from receipt (the fifth anniversary is still inside the period).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(d)
@export Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on a given day (s 264(d))?
GIVEN `the date the Secretary of State received the service` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State receive the service of process? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service (s 264(d))` IS
    NOT (`s 264(d) the Secretary of State is no longer required to retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service` `the day I am asking about`)

-- s 264(b). "Facts" includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
-- The list is open: an event, a determination or an action is a fact; for anything else the text does not say (the answer is then NOTHING).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(b)
@export Is this kind of fact one that a term of our agreement of merger or consolidation may depend on, under the meaning of "facts" in section 264(b) (s 264(b))?
GIVEN `the kind of fact` IS A `s 264(b) Kind of fact` @desc Which kind of fact? One of: the occurrence of an event under s 264(b); a determination by any person or body, including the corporation, under s 264(b); an action by any person or body, including the corporation, under s 264(b); something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 264(b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a fact a term of our agreement may depend on (s 264(b))` IS
    `s 264(b) the kind of fact is within the term facts` `the kind of fact`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(e)
@export Does this provision of the Law apply to a merger or consolidation between a corporation and a limited liability company (s 264(e))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `s 264(e) Provision applied by reference` @desc Which provision? One of: s 251(d) to (f) as applied by s 264(e); s 255(c) second sentence and (d) to (f) as applied by s 264(e); ss 259 to 261 as applied by s 264(e); s 328 as applied by s 264(e)
      `it is applicable to my merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision applicable to your merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision apply to a merger between a corporation and a limited liability company (s 264(e))` IS
    `s 264(e) the provision applies to the merger or consolidation` `the provision` `it is applicable to my merger or consolidation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(f)
@export Does section 264 stop my corporation merging into a limited liability company because its charitable status would be lost or impaired (s 264(f))?
GIVEN `the kind of my corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it? One of: a stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; a charitable nonstock corporation
      `my corporation would be merged into the limited liability company and would not survive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your corporation be merged into the limited liability company, so that it does not continue as the surviving corporation?
      `its charitable status would be lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the merger cause its charitable status to be lost or impaired?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 264 stop my charitable nonstock corporation merging into a limited liability company (s 264(f))` IS
    `s 264(f) the section does not authorize the merger of the charitable nonstock corporation into the limited liability company` `the kind of my corporation` `my corporation would be merged into the limited liability company and would not survive` `its charitable status would be lost or impaired`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 264(f)
@export May a limited liability company be merged into my charitable nonstock corporation, which continues as the surviving corporation (s 264(f))?
GIVEN `the kind of my corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it? One of: a stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; a charitable nonstock corporation
      `my corporation continues as the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your corporation continue as the surviving corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a limited liability company be merged into my charitable nonstock corporation (s 264(f))` IS
    `s 264(f) the limited liability company may be merged into the charitable nonstock corporation` `the kind of my corporation` `my corporation continues as the surviving corporation`


§ `s 265 -- my entity converting to a corporation of this State`

-- This group arises only if an entity other than a Delaware corporation is converting to a corporation of this State, or has done so.

-- s 265(a). An "other entity": a limited liability company, statutory trust, business trust or association, real estate investment trust, common-law trust or any other unincorporated business including a partnership, or a foreign corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(a)
@export Is my entity an "other entity" that may convert to a corporation of this State (s 265(a))?
GIVEN `what my entity is` IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes` @desc What kind of entity is it? Choose the description that fits.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my entity an other entity that may convert to a corporation of this State (s 265(a))` IS
    `s 265(a) the term other entity` (`dg8 seat the entity described` `what my entity is`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(b)
@export Have we converted to a corporation of this State by filing the two certificates as section 265(b) requires (s 265(b))?
GIVEN `what my entity is` IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes` @desc What kind of entity is it? Choose the description that fits.
      `the conversion was approved as subsection (h) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the conversion approved in the way subsection (h) requires? (Ask the question under section 265(h) below.)
      `the certificate of conversion was executed and filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of conversion to corporation executed in accordance with subsection (i) and filed in accordance with section 103?
      `the certificate of incorporation was executed, acknowledged and filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of incorporation executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103?
      `the two certificates were filed simultaneously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the two certificates filed simultaneously in the office of the Secretary of State?
      `the certificates are to be effective upon filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the certificates to become effective upon their filing, as section 103(d) permits?
      `each certificate provides the same effective date or time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not effective upon filing: does each certificate provide for the same effective date or time in accordance with section 103(d)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have we converted to a corporation of this State by filing as section 265(b) requires (s 265(b))` IS
    `s 265(b) the other entity has converted to a corporation of this State by filing as the subsection requires` (`dg8 seat the entity described` `what my entity is`) `the conversion was approved as subsection (h) requires` `the certificate of conversion was executed and filed` `the certificate of incorporation was executed, acknowledged and filed` `the two certificates were filed simultaneously` `the certificates are to be effective upon filing` `each certificate provides the same effective date or time`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(c)
@export Does our certificate of conversion to corporation state everything section 265(c) requires (s 265(c))?
GIVEN `the jurisdiction of my entity has changed since it first came into being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the jurisdiction of the other entity changed since it first came into being?
      `a plan of conversion is adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a plan of conversion adopted under subsection (k)?
      `the certificate states the date and place the entity first came into being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the date on which and jurisdiction where the other entity was first created, incorporated, formed or otherwise came into being?
      `the certificate states the jurisdiction immediately before the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the jurisdiction has changed: does the certificate state its jurisdiction immediately prior to its conversion to a domestic corporation?
      `the certificate states the name and type of entity before the filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name and type of entity of the other entity immediately prior to the filing of the certificate?
      `the certificate states the name of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name of the corporation as set forth in its certificate of incorporation filed under subsection (b)?
      `the certificate states that the plan will be approved before it takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a plan of conversion is adopted: does the certificate state that all provisions of the plan shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of the certificate in accordance with all law applicable to the other entity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our certificate of conversion state what section 265(c) requires (s 265(c))` IS
    `s 265(c) the certificate of conversion to corporation states what the subsection requires` `the jurisdiction of my entity has changed since it first came into being` `a plan of conversion is adopted` `the certificate statements`
    WHERE
        `the certificate statements` MEANS `s 265(c) Statements in the certificate of conversion to corporation` WITH
            `s 265(c)(1) the certificate states the date on which and jurisdiction where the other entity was first created, incorporated, formed or otherwise came into being` IS `the certificate states the date and place the entity first came into being`
            `s 265(c)(1) the certificate states the jurisdiction of the other entity immediately prior to its conversion to a domestic corporation` IS `the certificate states the jurisdiction immediately before the conversion`
            `s 265(c)(2) the certificate states the name and type of entity of the other entity immediately prior to the filing of the certificate` IS `the certificate states the name and type of entity before the filing`
            `s 265(c)(3) the certificate states the name of the corporation as set forth in its certificate of incorporation filed in accordance with subsection (b)` IS `the certificate states the name of the corporation`
            `s 265(c)(4) the certificate states that all provisions of the plan of conversion shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of the certificate in accordance with all law applicable to the other entity, including any approval required under that law for the authorization of the type of corporate action specified in the plan` IS `the certificate states that the plan will be approved before it takes effect`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(d)
@export Has the other entity been converted to a corporation of this State on the day I am asking about (s 265(d))?
GIVEN `the effective date of the two certificates` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the certificate of conversion and the certificate of incorporation take effect? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my entity become a corporation of this State on the day I am asking about (s 265(d))` IS
    `s 265(d) the other entity has been converted to a corporation of this State` `the effective date of the two certificates` `the day I am asking about`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(d)
@export On what date is the existence of the corporation deemed to have commenced, notwithstanding section 106 (s 265(d))?
GIVEN `the date my entity began to exist where it was first formed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the other entity commence its existence in the jurisdiction where it was first created, formed, incorporated or otherwise came into being? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When is the existence of my corporation deemed to have begun (s 265(d))` IS
    `s 265(d) the date on which the existence of the corporation is deemed to have commenced` `the date my entity began to exist where it was first formed`

-- s 265(e). The conversion does not affect liabilities incurred before it, or any person's personal liability incurred before it. The subsection says nothing of those incurred afterwards (the answer is then NOTHING).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(e)
@export Is the conversion not deemed to affect an obligation, liability or personal liability of mine that was incurred before it (s 265(e))?
GIVEN `it was incurred before the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the obligation, liability or personal liability incurred before the conversion?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the conversion leave my earlier liability untouched (s 265(e))` IS
    `s 265(e) the conversion is not deemed to affect the obligation or liability` `it was incurred before the conversion`

-- s 265(f). The corporation is the same entity; its rights, property and debts due remain vested in it; title to real property is not impaired; creditors' rights and liens are preserved; debts and liabilities remain attached and enforceable against it; none of it is a transfer.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(f)
@export What follows once the conversion to a corporation of this State has become effective (s 265(f))?
GIVEN `the conversion has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the conversion become effective under section 265?
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 265(f) Effect of a conversion that has become effective`
DECIDE `What follows once my entity has converted to a corporation of this State (s 265(f))` IS
    `s 265(f) the effects of the conversion` `the conversion has become effective`

-- s 265(f). The creditor's claim against the corporation is the correlative of the debts remaining attached to it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(f)
@export Do the debts, liabilities and duties of the other entity remain attached to the corporation and enforceable against it (s 265(f))?
GIVEN `the conversion has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the conversion become effective under section 265?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the converted entity's debts remain enforceable against the corporation (s 265(f))` IS
    `s 265(f) the effect follows from the conversion` `all debts, liabilities and duties of the other entity remain attached to the corporation and may be enforced against it as if incurred by it as a corporation under s 265(f)` `the conversion has become effective`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(g)
@export Is the converting other entity not required to wind up its affairs, pay its liabilities and distribute its assets (s 265(g))?
GIVEN `we have agreed otherwise for the purposes of Delaware law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it otherwise agreed for all purposes of the laws of Delaware?
      `non-Delaware law requires otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does applicable non-Delaware law require otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my converting entity spared winding up (s 265(g))` IS
    `s 265(g) the converting other entity is not required to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets` `we have agreed otherwise for the purposes of Delaware law` `non-Delaware law requires otherwise`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(g)
@export Is the conversion a continuation of the existence of the other entity in the form of a corporation, and not a dissolution (s 265(g))?
GIVEN `we have agreed otherwise for the purposes of Delaware law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it otherwise agreed for all purposes of the laws of Delaware?
      `non-Delaware law requires otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does applicable non-Delaware law require otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the conversion a continuation and not a dissolution (s 265(g))` IS
    `s 265(g) the conversion is a continuation of the existence of the other entity in the form of a corporation and not a dissolution` `we have agreed otherwise for the purposes of Delaware law` `non-Delaware law requires otherwise`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(h)
@export Has the conversion been approved as section 265(h) requires (s 265(h))?
GIVEN `it was approved in the manner our governing writing or the law provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the conversion approved in the manner provided for by the document, instrument, agreement or other writing governing the internal affairs of the other entity and the conduct of its business, or by applicable law?
      `it was approved before the certificate of conversion became effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it approved before the certificate of conversion became effective under section 103?
      `the certificate of incorporation was approved by the same authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of incorporation approved by the same authorization as was required to approve the conversion?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the conversion been approved as section 265(h) requires (s 265(h))` IS
    `s 265(h) the conversion is approved as the subsection requires` `it was approved in the manner our governing writing or the law provides` `it was approved before the certificate of conversion became effective` `the certificate of incorporation was approved by the same authorization`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(i)
@export Was the certificate of conversion to corporation signed by a person authorized to sign it for the other entity (s 265(i))?
GIVEN `it was signed by a person authorized to sign it for the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it signed by a person who is authorized to sign the certificate of conversion to corporation on behalf of the other entity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the certificate of conversion signed as section 265(i) requires (s 265(i))` IS
    `s 265(i) the certificate of conversion to corporation is signed as the subsection requires` `it was signed by a person authorized to sign it for the entity`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(j)
@export May rights, securities or interests in the converting entity be given this treatment in the conversion (s 265(j))?
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `s 265(j) Treatment of a right, security or interest in the other entity` @desc What is to happen to them? One of: exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of the corporation of this State; exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of or interests in another domestic corporation or other entity; cancelled; any treatment that subsection (j) does not list
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the interests in my entity be exchanged, converted or cancelled this way (s 265(j))` IS
    `s 265(j) the treatment is permitted in connection with a conversion` `the treatment`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(k)
@export May our plan of conversion state this matter (s 265(k))?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 265(k) Matter a plan of conversion may state` @desc What matter? One of: the terms and conditions of the conversion under s 265(k)(i); that the certificate of incorporation of the converted corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the plan under s 265(k)(ii); the manner, if any, of exchanging or converting shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the other entity under s 265(k)(iii); any corporate action to be taken by the converted corporation in connection with the conversion under s 265(k)(iv); any details or provisions that are deemed desirable under s 265(k)(v); such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in a plan of conversion by the laws applicable to the other entity under s 265(k)(vi); any matter that subsection (k) does not list
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our plan of conversion state this matter (s 265(k))` IS
    `s 265(k) the plan of conversion may state the matter` `the matter`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(k)
@export Has each corporate action stated in our plan of conversion been approved as section 265(k)(iv) requires (s 265(k)(iv))?
GIVEN `the corporate action is stated in the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporate action stated in the plan of conversion?
      `it was approved under all law applicable to the other entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it approved in accordance with all law applicable to the other entity, including any approval required under that law for the type of corporate action?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporate action stated in our plan been approved as section 265(k)(iv) requires (s 265(k)(iv))` IS
    `s 265(k)(iv) the corporate action stated in the plan is approved as the subsection requires` `the corporate action is stated in the plan` `it was approved under all law applicable to the other entity`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(k)
@export May a term of our plan of conversion depend on facts ascertainable outside the plan (s 265(k))?
GIVEN `the term depends on facts outside the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term depend on facts ascertainable outside the plan?
      `the plan clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those facts operate on the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a term of our plan of conversion depend on facts outside the plan (s 265(k))` IS
    `s 265(k) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the plan` `the term depends on facts outside the plan` `the plan clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate`

-- s 265(k). "Facts" includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body. The list is open: an event, a determination or an action is a fact; for anything else the text does not say (the answer is then NOTHING).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(k)
@export Is this kind of fact one that a term of our plan of conversion may depend on, under the meaning of "facts" in section 265 (s 265(k))?
GIVEN `the kind of fact` IS A `s 265(k) Kind of fact` @desc Which kind of fact? One of: the occurrence of an event under s 265(k); a determination by any person or body, including the other entity or the converted corporation, under s 265(k); an action by any person or body, including the other entity or the converted corporation, under s 265(k); something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 265(k)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a fact a term of our plan of conversion may depend on (s 265(k))` IS
    `s 265(k) the kind of fact is within the term facts` `the kind of fact`

-- s 265(l). The corporation, its board, stockholders or members are subject to the deemed authorization: they need take no further action under the title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(l)
@export Is a corporate action set forth in our plan of conversion deemed authorized, adopted and approved, so that I need take no further action as director, stockholder or member (s 265(l))?
GIVEN `the action is set forth in a plan approved as subsection (k) provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporate action set forth in a plan of conversion approved in the manner provided for by subsection (k)?
      `the action is within the power of a corporation under Subchapter II` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporate action within the power of a corporation under Subchapter II of the Law (the powers of a corporation)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a corporate action in our plan need no further action by the board, stockholders or members (s 265(l))` IS
    `s 265(l) the corporate action is deemed authorized, adopted and approved and needs no further action of the board, stockholders or members` `the action is set forth in a plan approved as subsection (k) provides` `the action is within the power of a corporation under Subchapter II`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 265(l)
@export Does the certificate we must file under another section of the Law state that no further action is required, as section 265(l) requires (s 265(l))?
GIVEN `the deemed authorization applies to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the deemed authorization in section 265(l) apply to the corporate action?
      `the action requires a certificate under another section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the action require the filing of a certificate under another section of the Law?
      `the certificate states that no further action is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that in accordance with section 265 no action by the board of directors, stockholders, members or as otherwise required by the other section is required?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the certificate we file under another section as section 265(l) requires (s 265(l))` IS
    `s 265(l) the certificate filed under another section is as the subsection requires` `the deemed authorization applies to the action` `the action requires a certificate under another section` `the certificate states that no further action is required`


§ `s 266 -- my corporation converting to another entity`

-- This group arises only if a corporation of this State is converting, or has converted, to another entity.

-- s 266(a). A corporation of this State may convert to a limited liability company, statutory trust, business trust or association, real estate investment trust, common-law trust or any other unincorporated business including a partnership, or a foreign corporation (the list is read as closed: fork F12).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(a)
@export May my corporation convert to this kind of entity, once the conversion is authorized (s 266(a))?
GIVEN `the entity my corporation would become` IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes` @desc What kind of entity would it become? Choose the description that fits.
      `the conversion has been authorized in accordance with the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the conversion been authorized in accordance with section 266?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation convert to this entity (s 266(a))` IS
    `s 266(a) the corporation may convert to the entity` (`dg8 seat the entity described` `the entity my corporation would become`) `the conversion has been authorized in accordance with the section`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b)
@export Has our board of directors adopted the resolution section 266(b) requires for the conversion (s 266(b))?
GIVEN `the board adopted a resolution approving the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of directors adopt a resolution approving the conversion?
      `the resolution specifies the type of entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution specify the type of entity into which the corporation shall be converted?
      `the resolution recommends approval by the stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution recommend the approval of the conversion by the stockholders?
      `a plan of conversion is to be adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a plan of conversion to be adopted under subsection (l)?
      `the plan was approved together with the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was the plan approved together with the resolution approving the conversion?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the board adopted the resolution section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))` IS
    `s 266(b) the board of directors has adopted the resolution the subsection requires` `the board adopted a resolution approving the conversion` `the resolution specifies the type of entity` `the resolution recommends approval by the stockholders` `a plan of conversion is to be adopted` `the plan was approved together with the resolution`

-- s 266(b). Due notice is to be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting. The stockholder's claim to notice is the corporation's duty to give it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b)
@export Am I entitled to due notice of the stockholders' meeting on the conversion, even if my stock is nonvoting (s 266(b))?
GIVEN `I hold stock of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold stock of the corporation, voting or nonvoting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to notice of the meeting on the conversion (s 266(b))` IS
    `s 266(b) the holder of stock is entitled to due notice of the meeting` `I hold stock of the corporation`

-- s 266(b). At least 20 days before the date of the meeting; read inclusively, so notice on the 20th day before is in time.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b)
@export Was notice of the meeting given to me in time and in the form section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))?
GIVEN `the notice states the time and purpose of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the time and purpose of the meeting?
      `the notice was sent to my address on the corporation's records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent to you at the address at which you appear on the records of the corporation?
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was notice of the meeting given to me as section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))` IS
    `s 266(b) notice of the meeting was given to the holder as the subsection requires` `the notice states the time and purpose of the meeting` `the notice was sent to my address on the corporation's records` `the date the notice was given` `the date of the meeting`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b)
@export Was the resolution submitted to the stockholders at an annual or special meeting, and considered and voted on there (s 266(b))?
GIVEN `it was submitted at an annual or special meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution submitted to the stockholders at an annual or special meeting?
      `it was considered and a vote taken there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the meeting, was the resolution considered and a vote taken for its adoption or rejection?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the resolution put to the stockholders as section 266(b) requires (s 266(b))` IS
    `s 266(b) the resolution was put to the stockholders as the subsection requires` `it was submitted at an annual or special meeting` `it was considered and a vote taken there`

-- s 266(b). A majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote: more than half. NOTHING if the counts cannot be a vote (no outstanding stock, or more votes cast than there are).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b)
@export Does the vote of the stockholders carry the resolution approving the conversion (s 266(b))?
GIVEN `the number of votes cast for the adoption of the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast for the adoption of the resolution?
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does the outstanding stock entitled to vote on it carry in all? (Count votes, not shares, if a share carries more or less than one vote.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the stockholders' vote carry the resolution (s 266(b))` IS
    `s 266(b) the vote of the stockholders carries the resolution` `the number of votes cast for the adoption of the resolution` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote`

-- s 266(b). The stockholder's approval is a condition of authorizing the conversion; the corporation cannot make the stockholder a general partner without it.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b)
@export Must I approve the conversion because I would become a general partner of the partnership (s 266(b))?
GIVEN `the corporation is converting to a partnership with general partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation converting to a partnership having 1 or more general partners?
      `I will become a general partner of the partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you, as a stockholder, become a general partner of that partnership as a result of the conversion?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I approve the conversion because I would become a general partner (s 266(b))` IS
    `s 266(b) the stockholder must approve the conversion` `the corporation is converting to a partnership with general partners` `I will become a general partner of the partnership`

-- s 266(b) and (i). If no shares had been issued, no vote of stockholders is necessary and the board's resolution suffices.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(b)
@export Is the conversion authorized by the board and the stockholders under section 266(b) and (i) (s 266(b))?
GIVEN `the board adopted the resolution the subsection requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of directors adopt the resolution section 266(b) requires?
      `no shares of stock had been issued before the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had no shares of the corporation's stock been issued before the board adopted the resolution approving the conversion?
      `the number of votes cast for the adoption of the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast for the adoption of the resolution?
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does the outstanding stock entitled to vote on it carry in all?
      `the corporation is converting to a partnership with general partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation converting to a partnership having 1 or more general partners?
      `a stockholder will become a general partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will any stockholder become a general partner of that partnership as a result of the conversion?
      `each such stockholder has approved the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each such stockholder approved the conversion? (Answer yes if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the conversion authorized by the board and the stockholders (s 266(b))` IS
    `s 266(b) the conversion is authorized by the board and the stockholders` `the board adopted the resolution the subsection requires` `no shares of stock had been issued before the resolution` `the number of votes cast for the adoption of the resolution` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` `the corporation is converting to a partnership with general partners` `a stockholder will become a general partner` `each such stockholder has approved the conversion`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)
@export Must my corporation file a certificate of conversion with the Secretary of State because it is converting to an entity of another jurisdiction (s 266(c))?
GIVEN `the new entity is formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the entity into which the corporation converts be organized, formed or created under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation file a certificate of conversion with the Secretary of State (s 266(c))` IS
    `s 266(c) the corporation must file a certificate of conversion with the Secretary of State` `the new entity is formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)
@export Is our certificate of conversion executed and does it certify everything section 266(c) requires (s 266(c))?
GIVEN `the name of the corporation has been changed since it was originally incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the name of the corporation been changed since it was originally incorporated?
      `a plan of conversion is adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a plan of conversion adopted under subsection (l)?
      `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate executed in accordance with section 103 of the Law?
      `the certificate certifies the name of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate certify the name of the corporation?
      `the certificate certifies the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the name has been changed: does the certificate certify the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated?
      `the certificate certifies the date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate certify the date of filing of the corporation's original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State?
      `the certificate certifies the name and jurisdiction of the new entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate certify the name and jurisdiction of the entity to which the corporation shall be converted?
      `the certificate certifies that the conversion has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate certify that the conversion has been approved in accordance with section 266?
      `the certificate certifies the agreement to be served with process in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate certify the corporation's agreement that it may be served with process in Delaware in any action, suit or proceeding to enforce an obligation arising while it was a corporation of this State or an obligation of the other entity arising from the conversion, including appraisal proceedings under section 262?
      `the certificate certifies the irrevocable appointment of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate certify that the corporation irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such action, suit or proceeding?
      `the certificate certifies the address for the Secretary of State to mail process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate certify the address to which a copy of the process shall be mailed to the corporation by the Secretary of State?
      `the certificate certifies that the plan will be approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a plan of conversion is adopted: does the certificate certify that all provisions of the plan shall be approved in accordance with section 266?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our certificate of conversion as section 266(c) requires (s 266(c))` IS
    `s 266(c) the certificate of conversion is as the subsection requires` `the certificate was executed in accordance with section 103` (`s 266(c) the certificate of conversion certifies what the subsection requires` `the name of the corporation has been changed since it was originally incorporated` `a plan of conversion is adopted` `the certifications`)
    WHERE
        `the certifications` MEANS `s 266(c) Certifications in the certificate of conversion` WITH
            `s 266(c)(1) the certificate certifies the name of the corporation` IS `the certificate certifies the name of the corporation`
            `s 266(c)(1) the certificate certifies the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated` IS `the certificate certifies the name under which the corporation was originally incorporated`
            `s 266(c)(2) the certificate certifies the date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State` IS `the certificate certifies the date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation`
            `s 266(c)(3) the certificate certifies the name and jurisdiction of the entity to which the corporation shall be converted` IS `the certificate certifies the name and jurisdiction of the new entity`
            `s 266(c)(4) the certificate certifies that the conversion has been approved in accordance with the provisions of the section` IS `the certificate certifies that the conversion has been approved`
            `s 266(c)(5) the certificate certifies the agreement of the corporation that it may be served with process in the State of Delaware in any action, suit or proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the corporation arising while it was a corporation of this State or of any obligation of the other entity arising from the conversion, including any suit or other proceeding to enforce the right of any stockholders as determined in appraisal proceedings pursuant to § 262` IS `the certificate certifies the agreement to be served with process in Delaware`
            `s 266(c)(5) the certificate certifies that the corporation irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such action, suit or proceeding` IS `the certificate certifies the irrevocable appointment of the Secretary of State`
            `s 266(c)(6) the certificate certifies the address to which a copy of the process shall be mailed to the corporation by the Secretary of State` IS `the certificate certifies the address for the Secretary of State to mail process`
            `s 266(c)(7) the certificate certifies that all provisions of the plan of conversion shall be approved in accordance with the section` IS `the certificate certifies that the plan will be approved`

-- s 266(c)(5). The claimant's power to serve the Secretary of State is the converted entity's liability to be served there (fork F7).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)(5)
@export May I serve process on the Secretary of State, as agent of the entity my corporation converted into, in my proceeding (s 266(c)(5))?
GIVEN `the new entity is formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity into which the corporation converted organized, formed or created under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
      `my proceeding is to enforce the corporation's obligation or the entity's obligation from the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your proceeding to enforce an obligation of the corporation arising while it was a corporation of this State, or an obligation of the other entity arising from the conversion (including an appraisal suit)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I serve process on the Secretary of State to sue the converted entity (s 266(c)(5))` IS
    `s 266(c)(5) process may be served on the Secretary of State as agent of the converted entity` `the new entity is formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware` `my proceeding is to enforce the corporation's obligation or the entity's obligation from the conversion`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)(6)
@export May I serve process on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 266(c)(6))?
GIVEN `I serve by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you serve the process by electronic transmission?
      `I serve as the Secretary of State prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you serve it as the Secretary of State has prescribed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I serve the Secretary of State by electronic transmission (s 266(c)(6))` IS
    `s 266(c)(6) the means of serving process on the Secretary of State is permitted` `I serve by electronic transmission` `I serve as the Secretary of State prescribes`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)(6)
@export Must the Secretary of State forthwith notify the converted entity by letter of the service (s 266(c)(6))?
GIVEN `process has been served on the Secretary of State under paragraph (c)(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has process been served on the Secretary of State under section 266(c)(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary of State notify the converted entity by letter (s 266(c)(6))` IS
    `s 266(c)(6) the Secretary of State must forthwith notify the converted entity by letter` `process has been served on the Secretary of State under paragraph (c)(5)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)(6)
@export To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter of notice to the converted entity (s 266(c)(6))?
GIVEN `the address the converted entity specified` IS A STRING @desc What address did the converted entity specify for the Secretary of State to mail process to?
      `the addresses designated in writing since, oldest first` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc What different addresses has it since designated in writing to the Secretary of State, oldest first? (An empty list if none.)
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter to the converted entity (s 266(c)(6))` IS
    `s 266(c)(6) the address to which the Secretary of State must mail the letter` `the address the converted entity specified` `the addresses designated in writing since, oldest first`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)(6)
@export Was the Secretary of State's letter to the converted entity sent as the Law requires (s 266(c)(6))?
GIVEN `it was sent by a mail or courier service with records of mailing and signed delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient?
      `it enclosed a copy of the process and papers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the letter enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the Secretary of State's letter to the converted entity sent as section 266(c)(6) requires (s 266(c)(6))` IS
    `s 266(c)(6) the letter is sent as the subsection requires` `it was sent by a mail or courier service with records of mailing and signed delivery` `it enclosed a copy of the process and papers`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)(6)
@export Have I done what the Law requires of a plaintiff who serves the Secretary of State on a converted corporation (s 266(c)(6))?
GIVEN `I served process and papers in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve process and any other papers in duplicate?
      `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under the subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected under section 266(c)(6)?
      `I paid the Secretary of State the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done what section 266(c)(6) requires of a plaintiff (s 266(c)(6))` IS
    `s 266(c)(6) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires of a plaintiff` `I served process and papers in duplicate` `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under the subsection` `I paid the Secretary of State the prescribed fee`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)(6)
@export Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs if I prevail (s 266(c)(6))?
GIVEN `I prevail in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you prevail in the proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the fee I pay the Secretary of State on a converted corporation be taxed as costs (s 266(c)(6))` IS
    `s 266(c)(6) the fee is taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding` `I prevail in the proceeding`

-- s 266(c)(6). The Secretary of State need not retain the record longer than 5 years from receipt (the fifth anniversary is still inside the period).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(c)(6)
@export Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service of process on a given day (s 266(c)(6))?
GIVEN `the date the Secretary of State received the service` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State receive the service of process? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of the service on the converted entity (s 266(c)(6))` IS
    NOT (`s 266(c)(6) the Secretary of State is no longer required to retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service` `the day I am asking about`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(d)
@export Has my corporation ceased to exist as a corporation of this State on the day I am asking about (s 266(d))?
GIVEN `the certificate of conversion to non-Delaware entity was filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of conversion to non-Delaware entity filed in accordance with subsection (c)?
      `all fees prescribed under the Law have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all fees prescribed under the Law been paid to the Secretary of State?
      `the date the certificate of conversion becomes effective` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the certificate become effective in accordance with section 103? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation ceased to exist as a corporation of this State (s 266(d))` IS
    `s 266(d) the corporation has ceased to exist as a corporation of this State` `the certificate of conversion to non-Delaware entity was filed` `all fees prescribed under the Law have been paid` `the date the certificate of conversion becomes effective` `the day I am asking about`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(d)
@export Is a copy of the certificate of conversion certified by the Secretary of State prima facie evidence of the conversion out of Delaware (s 266(d))?
GIVEN `the copy is certified by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy certified by the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a certified copy of the certificate of conversion prima facie evidence of the conversion (s 266(d))` IS
    `s 266(d) the copy is prima facie evidence of the conversion out of the State of Delaware` `the copy is certified by the Secretary of State`

-- s 266(e). The subsection says nothing of those incurred afterwards (the answer is then NOTHING).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(e)
@export Is the conversion out of Delaware not deemed to affect an obligation, liability or personal liability of mine incurred before it (s 266(e))?
GIVEN `it was incurred before the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the obligation, liability or personal liability incurred before the conversion?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the conversion leave my earlier liability untouched (s 266(e))` IS
    `s 266(e) the conversion is not deemed to affect the obligation or liability` `it was incurred before the conversion`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(e)
@export Is the conversion not deemed to affect the choice of law applicable to the corporation for matters arising before it (s 266(e))?
GIVEN `the matter arose before the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the matter arise before the conversion?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the conversion leave the choice of law for earlier matters untouched (s 266(e))` IS
    `s 266(e) the conversion is not deemed to affect the choice of law applicable to the matter` `the matter arose before the conversion`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(f)
@export Is the converting corporation not required to wind up its affairs, pay its liabilities and distribute its assets (s 266(f))?
GIVEN `a resolution of conversion provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a resolution of conversion adopted in accordance with section 266 provide otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my converting corporation spared winding up (s 266(f))` IS
    `s 266(f) the converting corporation is not required to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets` `a resolution of conversion provides otherwise`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(f)
@export Does the conversion not constitute a dissolution of my corporation (s 266(f))?
GIVEN `a resolution of conversion provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a resolution of conversion adopted in accordance with section 266 provide otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the conversion not a dissolution of my corporation (s 266(f))` IS
    `s 266(f) the conversion does not constitute a dissolution of the corporation` `a resolution of conversion provides otherwise`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(g)
@export May shares of the converting corporation be given this treatment in the conversion (s 266(g))?
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `s 266(g) Treatment of shares of stock of the corporation` @desc What is to happen to them? One of: exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the entity to which the corporation is being converted; exchanged for or converted into cash, property, shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, another domestic corporation or other entity; cancelled under s 266(g); any treatment that subsection (g) does not list
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my shares be exchanged, converted or cancelled this way (s 266(g))` IS
    `s 266(g) the treatment is permitted in connection with a conversion` `the treatment`

-- s 266(h). The new entity is the same entity; rights, property and debts due remain vested in it; title to real property is not impaired; creditors' rights and liens are preserved; debts and liabilities remain attached and enforceable against it; none of it is a transfer.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(h)
@export What follows once the conversion of my corporation to another entity has become effective (s 266(h))?
GIVEN `the conversion has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the conversion become effective under section 266?
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 266(h) Effect of a conversion that has become effective`
DECIDE `What follows once my corporation has converted to another entity (s 266(h))` IS
    `s 266(h) the effects of the conversion` `the conversion has become effective`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(i)
@export Is no vote of stockholders necessary to authorize the conversion because no shares had been issued (s 266(i))?
GIVEN `no shares of stock had been issued before the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had no shares of the corporation's stock been issued before the board adopted the resolution approving the conversion?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a vote of stockholders unnecessary because no shares have been issued (s 266(i))` IS
    `s 266(i) no vote of stockholders is necessary to authorize the conversion` `no shares of stock had been issued before the resolution`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(j)
@export Does section 266 stop my charitable nonstock corporation converting into another entity because its charitable status would be lost or impaired (s 266(j))?
GIVEN `the kind of my corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it? One of: a stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; a charitable nonstock corporation
      `its charitable status would be lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the conversion cause its charitable status to be lost or impaired?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 266 stop my charitable nonstock corporation converting (s 266(j))` IS
    `s 266(j) the section does not authorize the conversion of the charitable nonstock corporation` `the kind of my corporation` `its charitable status would be lost or impaired`

-- s 266(k). A corporation incorporated before August 1, 2022 ("before": 1 August itself is not); an agreement in effect on or before August 1, 2022 ("on or before": 1 August itself is).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(k)
@export Is a provision of my corporation's certificate of incorporation or of an agreement with its stockholders that restricts a merger deemed to apply to a conversion (s 266(k))?
GIVEN `where the restriction sits` IS A `s 266(k) Where the restriction on a merger or consolidation sits` @desc Where is the restriction? One of: a provision of the certificate of incorporation under s 266(k); a provision in a voting trust agreement or other written agreement between the corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders under s 266(k)
      `the date the corporation was incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the corporation incorporated? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the agreement came into effect` IS A DATE @desc If the restriction is in an agreement: on what date did the agreement come into effect? (YYYY-MM-DD; any date if it is in the certificate)
      `the provision restricts, conditions or prohibits a merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision restrict, condition or prohibit the consummation of a merger or consolidation?
      `the certificate or the agreement expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation or the agreement expressly provide that the restriction does not apply to a conversion?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a restriction on mergers in my certificate or agreement apply to a conversion (s 266(k))` IS
    `s 266(k) the provision is deemed to apply to a conversion as if it were a merger or consolidation` `where the restriction sits` `the date the corporation was incorporated` `the date the agreement came into effect` `the provision restricts, conditions or prohibits a merger or consolidation` `the certificate or the agreement expressly provides otherwise`

-- s 266(l). "Facts" includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body. The list is open: an event, a determination or an action is a fact; for anything else the text does not say (the answer is then NOTHING).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(l)
@export Is this kind of fact one that a term of our plan of conversion of the corporation may depend on, under the meaning of "facts" in section 266 (s 266(l))?
GIVEN `the kind of fact` IS A `s 266(l) Kind of fact` @desc Which kind of fact? One of: the occurrence of an event under s 266(l); a determination by any person or body, including the entity to which the corporation is being converted or the converting corporation, under s 266(l); an action by any person or body, including the entity to which the corporation is being converted or the converting corporation, under s 266(l); something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 266(l)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a fact a term of our plan of conversion of the corporation may depend on (s 266(l))` IS
    `s 266(l) the kind of fact is within the term facts` `the kind of fact`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(l)
@export May our corporation's plan of conversion state this matter (s 266(l))?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 266(l) Matter a plan of conversion may state` @desc What matter? One of: the terms and conditions of the conversion under s 266(l)(i); that the document governing the internal affairs of the entity to which the corporation is being converted shall be as set forth in an attachment to the plan under s 266(l)(ii); the manner, if any, of exchanging or converting shares of stock of the converting corporation under s 266(l)(iii); any details or provisions that are deemed desirable under s 266(l)(iv); such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in a plan of conversion by the laws applicable to the entity to which the corporation is being converted under s 266(l)(v); any matter that subsection (l) does not list
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our plan of conversion state this matter (s 266(l))` IS
    `s 266(l) the plan of conversion may state the matter` `the matter`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 266(l)
@export May a term of our corporation's plan of conversion depend on facts ascertainable outside the plan (s 266(l))?
GIVEN `the term depends on facts outside the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term depend on facts ascertainable outside the plan?
      `the plan clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those facts operate on the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a term of our corporation's plan of conversion depend on facts outside the plan (s 266(l))` IS
    `s 266(l) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the plan` `the term depends on facts outside the plan` `the plan clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate`


§ `s 267 -- a parent entity merging my corporation`

-- This group arises only if an entity that owns most of the stock of a corporation of this State is merging it under the short-form rule of section 267.

-- s 267(d)(2). "Entity" for this section only. A corporation is not an entity here.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(d)(2)
@export Is the parent that owns my corporation an "entity" within the meaning of section 267 (s 267(d)(2))?
GIVEN `what the parent is` IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes` @desc What kind of entity is it? Choose the description that fits.
      `it has members or outstanding shares or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have members, or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest? (Matters for a trust, an association or another unincorporated enterprise.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the parent an entity within section 267 (s 267(d)(2))` IS
    `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` (`dg8 seat the kind of entity described` `what the parent is`) `it has members or outstanding shares or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(d)(1)
@export Is this party a "constituent party", an entity or corporation to be merged under section 267 (s 267(d)(1))?
GIVEN `what the party is` IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes` @desc What kind of entity is it? Choose the description that fits.
      `it has members or outstanding shares or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have members, or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest?
      `it is to be merged under section 267` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to be merged under section 267?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a constituent party to the merger (s 267(d)(1))` IS
    `s 267(d)(1) the term constituent party` (`dg8 seat the kind of entity described` `what the party is`) `it has members or outstanding shares or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest` `it is to be merged under section 267`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(d)(3)
@export Is this instrument "governing documents" of the entity for section 267 (s 267(d)(3))?
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `s 267(d)(3) Instrument` @desc What is it? One of: a partnership agreement under s 267(d)(3); a limited liability company agreement under s 267(d)(3); articles of association under s 267(d)(3); any other instrument containing the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized under s 267(d)(3); an instrument that does not contain the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized under s 267(d)(3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this instrument governing documents for section 267 (s 267(d)(3))` IS
    `s 267(d)(3) the term governing documents` `the instrument`

-- s 267(a)(1). The test is "each class" of those that would be entitled to vote on the merger; one class stands for all of them: the one the parent owns the smallest share of (if it reaches 90 percent of that class it reaches it in every such class). Assumed, not ruled. NOTHING if there is no class to test or the counts cannot be a holding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export Does the parent entity own at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of the class of my corporation's stock that it owns the smallest share of (s 267(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation has the section 251(g)(7) provision in its certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have in its certificate of incorporation the provision required by section 251(g)(7)(A) and (B) of the Law?
      `the class has outstanding shares that would be entitled to vote on the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the class have outstanding shares that, apart from section 267, would be entitled to vote on the merger?
      `the number of outstanding shares of that class` IS A NUMBER @desc Take the class of stock the parent owns the smallest share of, among the classes that would be entitled to vote on the merger. How many shares of it are outstanding?
      `the number of those shares the parent owns` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class does the parent entity own?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the parent own at least 90 percent of every class of my corporation's stock (s 267(a)(1))` IS
    `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST `the class of stock the parent owns least of`)
    WHERE
        `the class of stock the parent owns least of` MEANS `s 267(a) Class of stock of a corporation` WITH
            `the corporation has in its certificate of incorporation the provision required by § 251(g)(7)(A) and (B)` IS `the corporation has the section 251(g)(7) provision in its certificate of incorporation`
            `there are outstanding shares of the class that, absent the subsection, would be entitled to vote on the merger` IS `the class has outstanding shares that would be entitled to vote on the merger`
            `the number of outstanding shares of the class` IS `the number of outstanding shares of that class`
            `the number of those shares owned by the entity` IS `the number of those shares the parent owns`

-- s 267(a). The parent's power to merge the corporation without a vote of its stockholders is the minority stockholder's liability to be merged; subsection (c) (below) gives the minority appraisal rights.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export May the parent entity merge my corporation into itself, or merge itself into a subsidiary, under section 267 (s 267(a))?
GIVEN `the corporation has the section 251(g)(7) provision in its certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have in its certificate of incorporation the provision required by section 251(g)(7)(A) and (B) of the Law?
      `the class has outstanding shares that would be entitled to vote on the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the class have outstanding shares that, apart from section 267, would be entitled to vote on the merger?
      `the number of outstanding shares of that class` IS A NUMBER @desc Take the class of stock the parent owns the smallest share of, among the classes that would be entitled to vote on the merger. How many shares of it are outstanding?
      `the number of those shares the parent owns` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class does the parent entity own?
      `the number of the corporations that are corporations of Delaware` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations to be merged are corporations of Delaware?
      `the law of the parent's or a foreign corporation's jurisdiction prohibits the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the laws of the jurisdiction under which the parent entity or a foreign corporation is formed or organized prohibit the merger?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the parent entity merge my corporation under section 267 (s 267(a))` IS
    `s 267(a) the entity may merge under this section` (`s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` (LIST `the class of stock the parent owns least of`)) (`s 267(a)(2) 1 or more of the corporations is a corporation of this State` `the number of the corporations that are corporations of Delaware`) `the law of the parent's or a foreign corporation's jurisdiction prohibits the merger`
    WHERE
        `the class of stock the parent owns least of` MEANS `s 267(a) Class of stock of a corporation` WITH
            `the corporation has in its certificate of incorporation the provision required by § 251(g)(7)(A) and (B)` IS `the corporation has the section 251(g)(7) provision in its certificate of incorporation`
            `there are outstanding shares of the class that, absent the subsection, would be entitled to vote on the merger` IS `the class has outstanding shares that would be entitled to vote on the merger`
            `the number of outstanding shares of the class` IS `the number of outstanding shares of that class`
            `the number of those shares owned by the entity` IS `the number of those shares the parent owns`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export Has the parent authorized the merger, and filed a certificate of ownership and merger, as section 267(a) requires (s 267(a))?
GIVEN `the parent authorized the merger under its governing documents and law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the parent entity authorize the merger in accordance with its governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized?
      `the certificate of ownership and merger was acknowledged and filed under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of ownership and merger acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 103?
      `the certificate was executed under the parent's governing documents and law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate executed in accordance with the entity's governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized?
      `the parent owns all the outstanding stock of all the corporations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the parent entity own all the outstanding stock of all the corporations party to the merger?
      `the certificate certifies that the merger was authorized under the parent's governing documents and law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate certify that the merger was authorized in accordance with the entity's governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized?
      `the certificate certifies the type of entity of each constituent entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate certify the type of entity of each constituent entity to the merger?
      `the certificate states the terms and conditions of the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the parent does not own all the stock: does the certificate state the terms and conditions of the merger, including the securities, cash, property or rights to be issued, paid, delivered or granted on surrender of each share not owned by the parent, or the cancellation of some or all of those shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the merger authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as section 267(a) requires (s 267(a))` IS
    `s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` `the parent authorized the merger under its governing documents and law` `the certificate of ownership and merger was acknowledged and filed under section 103` `the certificate was executed under the parent's governing documents and law` `the parent owns all the outstanding stock of all the corporations` `the certifications`
    WHERE
        `the certifications` MEANS `s 267(a) Certifications in the certificate of ownership and merger` WITH
            `s 267(a)(b)(i) the certificate certifies that the merger was authorized in accordance with the entity's governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which the entity is formed or organized` IS `the certificate certifies that the merger was authorized under the parent's governing documents and law`
            `s 267(a)(b)(ii) the certificate certifies the type of entity of each constituent entity to the merger` IS `the certificate certifies the type of entity of each constituent entity`
            `s 267(a)(A) the certificate states the terms and conditions of the merger, including the securities, cash, property or rights to be issued, paid, delivered or granted by the surviving constituent party upon surrender of each share not owned by the entity, or the cancellation of some or all of those shares` IS `the certificate states the terms and conditions of the merger`

-- s 267(a)(B). The question asks whether terms that make a holder a general partner are permitted; the fact "the terms make a holder a general partner" is therefore fixed at TRUE. Where the parent does not own all the stock, such terms are barred for a general partnership or a limited partnership but not for a limited liability partnership or limited liability limited partnership: the stockholder is immune from being made a general partner of the barred kinds.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export Can the terms and conditions of the merger make me, as a holder of stock, a general partner of the surviving entity (s 267(a))?
GIVEN `the parent owns all the outstanding stock of all the corporations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the parent entity own all the outstanding stock of all the corporations party to the merger? (No, if you are a minority stockholder.)
      `the kind of the surviving entity` IS A `dg8 seat Entity the person describes` @desc What kind of entity is the surviving entity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the terms of the merger make me a general partner (s 267(a))` IS
    `s 267(a)(B) the terms and conditions of the merger are permitted` `the parent owns all the outstanding stock of all the corporations` TRUE (`dg8 seat the kind of entity described` `the kind of the surviving entity`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export May a term of the merger depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate of ownership and merger (s 267(a))?
GIVEN `the term depends on facts outside the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate of ownership and merger?
      `the certificate clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those facts operate on the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a term of the merger depend on facts outside the certificate (s 267(a))` IS
    `s 267(a) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` `the term depends on facts outside the certificate` `the certificate clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export If the surviving constituent party is formed outside Delaware, do the terms of the merger have to obligate it as section 252(d) requires (s 267(a))?
GIVEN `the surviving constituent party is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving constituent party an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
      `the terms obligate it to provide the agreement and take the actions section 252(d) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving constituent party to provide the agreement, and take the actions, required by section 252(d)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 252(d) apply to the merger and bind the survivor (s 267(a))` IS
    `s 267(a) the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving constituent party as section 252(d) requires` `the surviving constituent party is formed outside Delaware` `the terms obligate it to provide the agreement and take the actions section 252(d) requires`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export Does the parent entity itself survive the merger (s 267(a))?
GIVEN `how the entity merges` IS A `s 267(a) How the entity merges` @desc How does the parent merge? One of: the entity merges the corporation or corporations into itself and assumes all of its or their obligations; the entity merges itself, or itself and 1 or more of the corporations, into 1 of the other corporations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Which party survives the merger (s 267(a))` IS
    `s 267(a) the entity is the surviving constituent party` `how the entity merges`

-- s 267(a). "Facts" includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body. The list is open: an event, a determination or an action is a fact; for anything else the text does not say (the answer is then NOTHING).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export Is this kind of fact one that a term of our merger may depend on, under the meaning of "facts" in section 267 (s 267(a))?
GIVEN `the kind of fact` IS A `s 267(a) Kind of fact` @desc Which kind of fact? One of: the occurrence of an event under s 267(a); a determination by any person or body, including the entity, under s 267(a); an action by any person or body, including the entity, under s 267(a); something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 267(a)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a fact a term of our merger may depend on (s 267(a))` IS
    `s 267(a) the kind of fact is within the term facts` `the kind of fact`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export Does section 252(d), on service of process, also apply to my merger under section 267 because the survivor is formed outside Delaware (s 267(a))?
GIVEN `the surviving constituent party is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving constituent party an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 252(d) also apply to a merger under section 267 (s 267(a))` IS
    `s 267(a) section 252(d) also applies to the merger` `the surviving constituent party is formed outside Delaware`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a)
@export In applying section 252(d) to my merger under section 267, is the word "corporation" read to include the parent entity (s 267(a))?
GIVEN `the surviving constituent party is formed outside Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving constituent party an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than Delaware?
      `how the entity merges` IS A `s 267(a) How the entity merges` @desc How does the parent merge? One of: the entity merges the corporation or corporations into itself and assumes all of its or their obligations; the entity merges itself, or itself and 1 or more of the corporations, into 1 of the other corporations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the word corporation in section 252(d) read to include the parent entity (s 267(a))` IS
    `s 267(a) the word corporation in section 252(d) is deemed to include the entity` `the surviving constituent party is formed outside Delaware` (`s 267(a) the entity is the surviving constituent party` `how the entity merges`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(b)
@export In a merger under section 267, how is this reference in a provision the section applies read (s 267(b))?
GIVEN `the reference` IS A `s 267(b) Reference in a provision applied by s 267(b)` @desc Which reference? One of: the words agreement of merger in s 251(e); the word corporation in ss 259 to 261; the word corporation in s 328
GIVETH A `s 267(b) How a reference is read`
DECIDE `How is this reference read in a merger under section 267 (s 267(b))` IS
    `s 267(b) the way the reference is read` `the reference`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(b)
@export Does this provision of the Law apply to a merger under section 267 (s 267(b))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `s 267(b) Provision applied by reference` @desc Which provision? One of: s 259 as applied by s 267(b); s 261 as applied by s 267(b); s 328 as applied by s 267(b); s 260 as applied by s 267(b); s 251(e) as applied by s 267(b)
      `it is applicable to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision applicable to your merger?
      `the surviving constituent party is a corporation of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving constituent party a corporation of Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision apply to a merger under section 267 (s 267(b))` IS
    `s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` `the provision` `it is applicable to the merger` `the surviving constituent party is a corporation of Delaware`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(b)
@export Does section 262 (appraisal) apply to a merger under section 267 (s 267(b))?
GIVEN `the parent owned all the stock of the Delaware corporation immediately before the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the parent entity own all of the stock of the Delaware corporation party to the merger immediately before the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 262 apply to a merger under section 267 (s 267(b))` IS
    `s 267(b) section 262 applies to the merger` `the parent owned all the stock of the Delaware corporation immediately before the merger`

-- s 267(c). The stockholder's appraisal right is the surviving party's liability to pay fair value as determined under section 262. Whether the stockholder meets section 262's own conditions is answered by the piece that encodes section 262.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(c)
@export As a stockholder of the Delaware corporation, do I have appraisal rights as set forth in section 262 in a merger under section 267 (s 267(c))?
GIVEN `the parent owned all the stock of the Delaware corporation immediately before the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the parent entity own all of the stock of the Delaware corporation party to the merger immediately before the merger? (No, if you hold shares the parent does not own.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have appraisal rights in a merger under section 267 (s 267(c))` IS
    `s 267(c) the stockholders of the Delaware corporation have appraisal rights as set forth in section 262` `the parent owned all the stock of the Delaware corporation immediately before the merger`


§ `s 268 -- the merger agreement, the surviving corporation's certificate and the disclosure schedules`

-- This group arises only if a corporation of this State is party to a merger agreement under the subchapter.

@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(a)
@export Does section 268(a) apply to my corporation, a constituent corporation in the merger (s 268(a))?
GIVEN `the agreement of merger was entered into under section 251(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement of merger entered into under section 251(g) of the Law (the holding-company merger)?
      `the agreement converts all the shares into cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide that all of the shares of capital stock of the constituent corporation issued and outstanding immediately before the merger becomes effective are to be converted into or exchanged for cash, property, rights or securities, excluding stock of the surviving corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 268(a) apply to my constituent corporation (s 268(a))` IS
    `s 268(a) the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` `the agreement of merger was entered into under section 251(g)` `the agreement converts all the shares into cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(a)(i)
@export May our board of directors approve an agreement of merger that includes no provision about the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation (s 268(a)(i))?
GIVEN `the agreement of merger was entered into under section 251(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement of merger entered into under section 251(g) of the Law (the holding-company merger)?
      `the agreement converts all the shares into cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide that all of the shares of capital stock of the constituent corporation issued and outstanding immediately before the merger becomes effective are to be converted into or exchanged for cash, property, rights or securities, excluding stock of the surviving corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board approve an agreement that is silent on the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation (s 268(a)(i))` IS
    `s 268(a)(i) the agreement approved by the board need not include any provision regarding the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation` (`s 268(a) the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` `the agreement of merger was entered into under section 251(g)` `the agreement converts all the shares into cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(a)(ii)
@export May this person adopt an amendment, or an amendment and restatement, of the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation (s 268(a)(ii))?
GIVEN `who` IS A `s 268(a)(ii) Who may adopt an amendment of the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation` @desc Who? One of: the board of directors of the constituent corporation; a person acting at the direction of the board of directors of the constituent corporation; the board of directors or governing body of a constituent entity whose shares or equity interests are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation; a person acting at the direction of the board of directors or governing body of such a constituent entity; any other person
      `the agreement of merger was entered into under section 251(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement of merger entered into under section 251(g) of the Law (the holding-company merger)?
      `the agreement converts all the shares into cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide that all of the shares of capital stock of the constituent corporation issued and outstanding immediately before the merger becomes effective are to be converted into or exchanged for cash, property, rights or securities, excluding stock of the surviving corporation?
      `the shares or equity interests of a constituent entity are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the terms of the agreement of merger, are the shares or equity interests of a constituent entity to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this person adopt an amendment of the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation (s 268(a)(ii))` IS
    `s 268(a)(ii) the person may adopt an amendment of the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation` `who` (`s 268(a) the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` `the agreement of merger was entered into under section 251(g)` `the agreement converts all the shares into cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation`) `the shares or equity interests of a constituent entity are to be converted into all of the shares of capital stock of the surviving corporation`

-- s 268(a)(iii). Where the subsection applies, no: such a change is not deemed an amendment to the agreement. Where it does not apply, the subsection says nothing (NOTHING).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(a)(iii)
@export Is a change to the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation deemed an amendment to the agreement of merger (s 268(a)(iii))?
GIVEN `the agreement of merger was entered into under section 251(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement of merger entered into under section 251(g) of the Law (the holding-company merger)?
      `the agreement converts all the shares into cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide that all of the shares of capital stock of the constituent corporation issued and outstanding immediately before the merger becomes effective are to be converted into or exchanged for cash, property, rights or securities, excluding stock of the surviving corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a change to the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation an amendment to the merger agreement (s 268(a)(iii))` IS
    `s 268(a)(iii) the alteration or change of the certificate of incorporation is deemed an amendment to the agreement of merger` (`s 268(a) the subsection applies to the constituent corporation` `the agreement of merger was entered into under section 251(g)` `the agreement converts all the shares into cash, property, rights or securities other than stock of the surviving corporation`)

-- s 268(b). Unless the agreement expressly provides otherwise, they are not part of it for the purposes of any provision of the title. NOTHING where the agreement provides otherwise or the document is not of that kind.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(b)
@export Are the disclosure schedules delivered with the merger agreement part of the agreement for the purposes of the Law (s 268(b))?
GIVEN `the document is a disclosure letter or schedule that qualifies the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a disclosure letter, disclosure schedules or similar document or instrument, delivered in connection with the agreement, that modifies, supplements, qualifies or makes exceptions to representations, warranties, covenants or conditions in the agreement?
      `the agreement expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement of merger or consolidation expressly provide otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the disclosure schedules part of the merger agreement for the Law (s 268(b))` IS
    `s 268(b) the disclosure schedule is part of the agreement for purposes of any provision of the title` `the document is a disclosure letter or schedule that qualifies the agreement` `the agreement expressly provides otherwise`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 268(b)
@export Do the disclosure schedules have the effects provided in the agreement (s 268(b))?
GIVEN `the document is a disclosure letter or schedule that qualifies the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a disclosure letter, disclosure schedules or similar document or instrument, delivered in connection with the agreement, that modifies, supplements, qualifies or makes exceptions to representations, warranties, covenants or conditions in the agreement?
      `the agreement expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement of merger or consolidation expressly provide otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the disclosure schedules have the effects the agreement gives them (s 268(b))` IS
    `s 268(b) the disclosure schedule has the effects provided in the agreement` `the document is a disclosure letter or schedule that qualifies the agreement` `the agreement expressly provides otherwise`
